course: dictionary
lesson: 3812
title: What is a forest?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A forest is a large area of land covered thickly with trees and plants. Read this: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» The word forests means big areas full of trees, and the macaws live in them.
explain: Forest has a second meaning, a picture meaning. «A forest of hands» means a large number of hands close together, like tall trees packed tightly in a forest. When you meet forest, ask yourself: is this a place full of trees, or a crowd of tall things?
explain: Forests are also places to be careful in. Stay on the paths, tell an adult where you are going, and never light fires in a dry forest. In fairy tales, the dark forest is often a place of danger and adventure.
fact: A forest is a large area of land covered thickly with trees and plants.
fact: «Forest» can also mean a large number of tall things close together, such as «a forest of hands».
fact: Forests are habitats, which means homes for many animals, plants and insects.
fact: Forests give us oxygen, store carbon and hold soil in place.
fact: Three main kinds are rainforest (hot, wet, near the equator), deciduous forest (trees lose their leaves in autumn) and coniferous forest (evergreen trees).
exercise: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» In this sentence, what is a forest? | A kind of bird that cracks nuts | A river full of fish | A small park with one tree | *A large area of land covered thickly with trees and plants
exercise: Which kind of forest has trees that lose their leaves in autumn? | Rainforest | *Deciduous forest | Coniferous forest | Desert
exercise: «A forest of hands» means what? | A wooden fence around a field | A group of trees with no leaves | A tall castle wall | *A large number of tall things close together
test: Which is a safety rule for a forest? | Light a fire to keep warm | *Stay on the paths and tell an adult where you go | Go off the path and wander alone | Climb to the top of the tallest tree
test: In fairy tales, what is the dark forest often? | *A place of danger and adventure | A busy city street | A cosy place for picnics | A shop full of sweets
exam: Which sentence uses forest to mean a large number of tall things close together? | The lions rested all day | *She raised a forest of hands to answer | Macaws crack palm nuts with their beaks | The taiga is cold and quiet
